  "disclosures": [
    "Everything here is devnet and synthetic test assets; there is no mainnet deployment, no issuer-backed share and no production liquidity.",
    "The program has never been security audited and has no formal verification; the reviews recorded here are scoped engineering reviews, not an audit certificate.",
    "The upgrade authority on the devnet program is retained by the approved wallet, which is a real trust assumption.",
    "Authenticated equity prices are excluded; the oracle is a labelled fixture publisher and the evidence says TEST PRICES.",
    "The residual venue is CrossFlow's own controlled constant-product test venue with test tokens; it is not Meteora, not Jupiter and not a market.",
    "The browser flow is exercised with an injected wallet stub and a stubbed RPC; the real Phantom extension flow and any hosting are untested.",
    "The economic comparison is modelled micro-USD under one frozen cost convention on synthetic scenarios; the cooperative gain is positive in only four of six eligible held-out scenarios and 36 of 72 sensitivity points.",
    "The service is a loopback, single-deployment, unauthenticated local operator tool; it holds no user key and never signs.",
    "No submission has been made and no public artefact has been published.",
    "There is no adversarial runtime matrix against the deployed instruction, and no unfamiliar-user or screen-reader review has been run.",
